% It is possible to receive d1 infinitely often. The alternation gives the parity game more than one
% priority, so the strategy computed by the symbolic solver comes from the attractor computations
% rather than from the degenerate single-priority case. Those pieces of the strategy are already
% restricted to one attractor layer, and determinizing them relies on a different argument (progress
% towards the target) than the arbitrary choice at the minimal rank.
nu X. mu Y. ((<r1(d1)>X) || (<true>Y))
